{
  "headline": "FDA's shortage list shows paclitaxel posted 2021-10-05 and still listed as of 2026-10-21 (61 months); our supply traces to Sagent label 5721b9bf naming plant GLAND (sponsor only) and an alternate Alembic plant with VAI 2024-03-08",
  "headline_cites": ["D6", "E6", "E8"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list shows paclitaxel first posted 2021-10-05 and still listed as of 2026-10-21, a duration of 61 months.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our Corvale sites use NDC 25021025550 labeled by Sagent Pharmaceuticals (label set 5721b9bf) which names plant GLAND with operations listed as sponsor only.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E3", "E5", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An alternate manufacturer, Alembic Pharmaceuticals Limited, operates a registered plant (FEI 3014866088) that received a VAI classification on 2024-03-08 per FDA inspection 1232189.",
      "cites": ["E8", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No FDA enforcement action at a registered plant precedes the 2021-10-05 posting for our labeled supply, so the root cause remains unverified in FDA's public records.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E6", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 21 vials of 6 mg/mL 50 mL at 3.5 vials per day (6 days on hand); Corvale General holds 81 vials at 3.1 per day (26.1 days on hand).",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked best option is to transfer 29 vials of 6 mg/mL 50 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, leaving General with two weeks' supply and bringing East to 14 days.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A secondary option transfers 4 vials from Corvale General to Corvale Lakeside (9.2 days on hand) to reach 14 days, and an alternate manufacturer (Abraxis BioScience, LLC) is not on FDA's shortage list today.",
      "cites": ["D8", "D9"]
    }
  ]
}
